        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(codex): cap compaction override warning cache via createDedupeCache",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes unbounded memory growth in the Codex app-server compaction override warning deduplication. The `warnedIgnoredCompactionOverrides` Set accumulated every warned override key forever with no eviction, TTL, or size cap.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nReplaced the unbounded `Set<string>` with `createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })`, imported from `openclaw/plugin-sdk/dedupe-runtime` per extension boundary policy. The `check()` method provides touch-on-read LRU semantics.\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo change for gateways handling fewer than 4 096 distinct ignored compaction-override keys. Gateways exceeding the cap may see one extra warning per evicted entry, a bounded trade-off versus the prior unbounded growth.\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Real-path proof — `embeddedAgentLog` writes to stderr through the real OpenClaw logging system\n\nThe script initializes the OpenClaw console logger (`loggingState.overrideSettings`), imports the actual `compact.js` module, and calls `maybeCompactCodexAppServerSession` twice with identical compaction config. The REAL `embeddedAgentLog` (not a mock) writes to stderr:\n\n```text\n$ node --import tsx compact-proof-real.mjs 2>&1\n\n[agent/embedded] ignoring OpenClaw compaction overrides for Codex app-server compaction; Codex uses native server-side compaction\n[agent/embedded] skipping codex app-server compaction for non-manual trigger\nFirst call: via real embeddedAgentLog.warn — warning emitted\n\n[agent/embedded] skipping codex app-server compaction for non-manual trigger\nSecond call (same config): via real embeddedAgentLog.warn — warning suppressed\n\nOK: deduplication works through REAL embeddedAgentLog\n```\n\n- First call: `warnIfIgnoringOpenClawCompactionOverrides` → real `embeddedAgentLog.warn` fires\n- Second call (same config): `createDedupeCache.check()` returns true → real `embeddedAgentLog.warn` suppressed\n\n### Cache cap and LRU eviction\n\n`createDedupeCache({ ttlMs: 0, maxSize: 4096 })` cap/eviction verified by unit tests:\n\n```text\n$ pnpm vitest run src/infra/dedupe.test.ts --reporter=verbose\n\n ✓ createDedupeCache > keeps entries indefinitely when ttlMs is zero or negative\n ✓ createDedupeCache > touches duplicate reads so the newest key survives max-size pruning\n ... 5 passed (5)\n```\n\n### Plugin boundary contract passes\n\n```text\n$ pnpm vitest run src/plugins/contracts/plugin-sdk-package-contract-guardrails.test.ts\n\n ✓ keeps extension sources on public sdk or local package seams  ... 22 passed (22)\n```\n\nAI-assisted: built with Codex",
